# FE — React & TypeScript component standards

`docs/architecture.md` **always wins** for stack-specific choices (routing, data layer, forms, CSS approach). This rule fills gaps when the architecture doc is silent.

---

## Imports & module boundaries

- Use **relative imports** or **aliases** exactly as the architecture doc defines. Do not import across layers the architect marked as forbidden (e.g. UI → server internals).
- **One primary UI component per file** unless the codebase already uses a different pattern; prefer **`export default`** for that component.
- For heavier prop models, colocate **`ComponentName.types.ts`** (or `types.ts` in the component folder) instead of bloating the component file.

---

## TypeScript

- Prefer **`type`** over **`interface`** (reserve `interface` for declaration merging / extends patterns only).
- **Do not use `React.FC`.** Type props explicitly on the function.
- Use **`??`** for nullish coalescing (not `||` when `0`, `''`, or `false` are valid values).
- Use **`!!`** or explicit comparisons for boolean coercion when needed.
- Avoid **`any`**; use `unknown` + narrowing if data shape is uncertain.

---

## Props & components

- **Destructure** props in the function parameters.
- Use **default parameter values** for optional props so the UI does not depend on `undefined` unless intentional.

---

## Hooks

- **No `async` directly in `useEffect`** — define an inner async function and call it; handle cancellation if needed.
- **Do not** call hooks conditionally, in loops, or after early returns that skip hook calls.
- Do **not** put `ref` objects in dependency arrays (use `.current` or stable callbacks per React docs).
- Use **`useCallback` / `useMemo`** only when justified (child wrapped in `memo`, stable reference required, or expensive pure derivation).
- Non-hook helpers must **not** be named with the `use` prefix.

---

## Data fetching & async

- Use the **data-fetching approach** named in `docs/architecture.md` (e.g. React Query, SWR, plain `fetch`). If unspecified, use simple `fetch` + `try/catch`.
- Always **`try/catch`** or **`.catch()`** for async; never swallow errors silently — log or surface per architecture.
- Prefer **`Promise.all`** for parallel independent requests; **`Promise.allSettled`** when partial failure is acceptable.

---

## Conditionals & readability

- Avoid **nested ternaries**; extract variables or small helpers.
- Prefer small **lookup objects** over long `switch` / `if` chains when mapping keys → UI.
- Use **`&&`** for simple conditional render when it improves clarity.

---

## Next.js (only if the project uses Next.js per architecture)

- Prefer **`next/image`** instead of raw `<img>` for optimized images.
- Treat **dynamic route / query params** as `string | string[] | undefined` — narrow safely (e.g. `Array.isArray(q) ? q[0] : q`).
- Prefer **`router.pathname`** / framework navigation APIs over manual `window.location` string hacks.

---

## Forms & validation

- Follow the **form library** in `docs/architecture.md` if specified. Otherwise: controlled inputs, validate on submit, show field-level errors accessibly.

---

## Accessibility

- Images: meaningful **`alt`** (empty `alt=""` only for decorative images).
- Inputs: associated **`<label>`** or `aria-label` / **`aria-describedby`** for error text.
- **Icon-only buttons**: `aria-label` describing the action.
- Links that open a new tab: make it obvious (text or **`aria-label`**) per product language.

---

## Styling (generic)

- Follow **CSS approach** in architecture (CSS Modules, Tailwind, etc.). Avoid magic numbers where design tokens exist; keep responsive behavior explicit.

---

## Security & env (FE boundary)

- **Never** hardcode secrets, API keys, or tokens — use **environment variables** as defined in architecture.
- Do not expose raw stack traces or internal errors in user-visible UI.

---

## Pre–Ready for Review (FE checklist)

- [ ] Matches acceptance criteria and `docs/architecture.md` patterns
- [ ] Hooks and TypeScript rules above respected
- [ ] Async paths have error handling
- [ ] Basic a11y: labels, alt, icon buttons
- [ ] No stray `console.log` in paths meant for demo/production
